From: OpenHarmony PC Adaptation <noreply@openharmony.io>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 07:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] llvm: avoid versioned shared-library symlinks on HarmonyOS

LLVM assigns VERSION and SOVERSION to explicit shared libraries whenever UNIX
is true. CMake then creates an unversioned symlink beside each real versioned
library. HMDFS cannot reliably create or follow those symlinks, so emit the
unversioned shared object as the single real artifact for both OHOS CMake
system spellings used by the official SDK and the Conan toolchain.

Origin: https://github.com/root-project/llvm-project/tree/cling-llvm20-20260119-01
Upstream-Status: Not-Submitted [contest adaptation]
Source-Commit: 6fb92ab985353ed71faec49beaaf5d111e041f8c
Modification-Layer: 1 (CMake module source)
Knowledge-Ref: E050
---
 llvm/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/llvm/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake b/llvm/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake
--- a/llvm/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake
+++ b/llvm/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake
@@ -721,6 +721,7 @@ function(llvm_add_library name)
     # Set SOVERSION on shared libraries that lack explicit SONAME
     # specifier, on *nix systems that are not Darwin.
-    if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT ARG_SONAME)
+    if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT ARG_SONAME
+        AND NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "^(OHOS|HarmonyOS)$")
       set_target_properties(${name}
         PROPERTIES
         # Since 18.1.0, the ABI version is indicated by the major and minor version.
